-- title:
--   A fibre model with cusp chart for X₀(N)
-- statement:
--   Fix a positive integer $N$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a prime $\ell$, a field $k$ of characteristic $\ell$, and a surjective ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$. Assume given modular polynomial data `data` for level $N$, that is a monic $\Phi \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(N) = \sum_{d \mid N,\ d \text{ squarefree}} N/d$ in $Y$ vanishing on the pair of $q$-expansions $(j, j_N)$; assume the relative degree of $k$-adjoin $\{j_q, j_{q,N}\}$ inside $k((q))$ over $k$-adjoin $\{j_q\}$ equals $\psi(N)$; assume the coefficient bound $\deg_X(\Phi.\mathrm{coeff}\, i) \le N(\psi(N) - i)$ for all $i$; and assume two lifting hypotheses: every $y$ in the reduced modular function field `modularFunctionFieldC k N` which satisfies a monic polynomial over $k[j_q]$ (respectively over $k[j_q^{-1}]$) is the image under `modularRedLocHom` of some element $f$ of the localisation `modularLocalized N A.toSubring red` of the subring generated by the constants from $A$ together with $j_q$ and $j_{q,N}$ at the complement of the reduction kernel, with $f$ satisfying a monic polynomial over $A[j_q]$ (respectively $A[j_q^{-1}]$). Then there exists a `FibreModel N A ℓ k red` — a pair of subrings $B_{\mathrm{fin}}, B_{\mathrm{inf}}$ of the Laurent base change of the full modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, containing the constants from $A$, with $\bar j, \bar j_N \in B_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and $\bar j^{-1} \in B_{\mathrm{inf}}$, each integral over the corresponding affine base ring, equipped with reduction homomorphisms $\pi_{\mathrm{fin}}, \pi_{\mathrm{inf}}$ into `modularFunctionFieldC k N` sending constants $a$ to $\mathrm{red}(a)$, $\bar j \mapsto j_q$, $\bar j_N \mapsto j_{q,N}$, $\bar j^{-1} \mapsto j_q^{-1}$, together with the further conditions recorded in the structure — which satisfies `CuspChart`: the element $\bar j_N \cdot (\bar j^{-1})^N$ lies in $B_{\mathrm{inf}}$ and is carried by $\pi_{\mathrm{inf}}$ to $j_{q,N} \cdot (j_q^{-1})^N$.
--
--   This is the inhabitation statement for the structures `FibreModel` and `FibreModel.CuspChart`: under the stated degree and lifting hypotheses, the two affine charts of a model of $X_0(N)$ over the valuation ring $A$, with their reductions to characteristic $\ell$ and with the cusp coordinate $t = j_N/j^N$ available on the chart at infinity, can be produced. It is used by [`ModularCurve.CharPModel.exists_fibreModel_cuspChart_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.CharPModel.exists_fibreModel_cuspChart_of_not_dvd), where the hypotheses are verified for residue characteristics not dividing the level.
